==English==

===Etymology===
{{suf|en|jog|er|id2=agent noun}}. The ethnic slur is a reference to [[w:Killing of Ahmaud Arbery|Ahmaud Arbery]], a black man who was killed by three white assailants while jogging in 2020. It is used mostly on the Internet as a substitute for the word {{m|en|nigger}}, where it bypasses most filters or bots that restrict certain keywords.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈd͡ʒɒ.ɡə(ɹ)/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-jogger.wav|Audio (UK)}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈd͡ʒɑɡɚ/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒɡə(ɹ)|s=2}}

